          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most damp bedrooms, the GE ADYR22LC is the dehumidifier we would buy: 22 pints a day under the current DOE test and the lowest published low-speed noise rating we found, 43 dBA. The Danby is the smart pick if you want app control and scheduling, the Honeywell is for light sleepers who want a true sleep mode, and the Pro Breeze PB-03 is for small rooms where silence matters more than capacity.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, measure first, because many bedrooms do not need a dehumidifier at all. If yours does, dry the room before bed with the door closed, empty the bucket at bedtime, place the unit away from your pillow and aim for 40 to 50 percent, not as low as it will go.
